  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="69c2a2b2-81d9-55fb-9121-c837bd5abd2a" activityNameId="5b8117e8-abaf-553b-a2be-25a31794bb16" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, paint, 0% water, to sanitary landfill</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, paint, 0% water, to sanitary landfill
Inventoried waste contains 100% paint (remains); . waste composition (wet, in ppm): upper heating value 10.86 MJ/kg; lower heating value 10.14 MJ/kg; H2O n.a.; O 290300; H 36288; C 651510; S n.a.; N n.a.; P n.a.; B n.a.; Cl 1600; Br n.a.; F n.a.; I n.a.; Ag n.a.; As 2.5; Ba n.a.; Cd 5.0622; Co 388.23; Cr 1040.7; Cu 59; Hg 0.6; Mn n.a.; Mo 38.619; Ni 15; Pb 15246; Sb n.a.; Se n.a.; Sn 256.78; V n.a.; Zn 3251.5; Be n.a.; Sc n.a.; Sr n.a.; Ti n.a.; Tl n.a.; W n.a.; Si n.a.; Fe n.a.; Ca n.a.; Al n.a.; K n.a.; Mg n.a.; Na n.a.; Share of carbon in waste that is biogenic 0%. Overall degradability of waste during 100 years: 1%.;; UUID: 8044d99b-e07b-4a80-9312-8b5bcc8e2b2e
Waste-specific short-term emissions to air via landfill gas incineration and landfill leachate. Burdens from treatment of short-term leachate (0-100a) in wastewater treatment plant (including WWTP sludge disposal in municipal incinerator). Long-term emissions from landfill to groundwater (after base lining failure). 
Location: Technology encountered in Switzerland in 2000. Landfill includes base seal, leachate collection system, treatment of leachate in municipal wastewater treatment plant.
Technology: Swiss municipal sanitary landfill for biogenic or untreated municipal waste ("reactive organic landfill"). Landfill gas and leachate collection system. Recultivation and monitoring for 150 years after closure.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Landfill model based on observed leachate concentrations in literature. Extrapolated to 60'000 years heeding chemical characteristics. Initial waste composition from various literature sources. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: uncertainty of waste input composition data derived from generic formula GSD(c) = N*ln(c)+1. Minimal long-term emissions are the emissions until the carbonate buffer in the landfill is used up. Mean long-term emissions are the emissions until the next glacial period occurs (in 60'000a) and the landfill is eroded. Maximal long-term emissions are the complete emissions of all landfilled material (except Cr).
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_8044d99b-e07b-4a80-9312-8b5bcc8e2b2e.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
